1
00:00:00,125 --> 00:00:02,040
How long
is a chain of us?

2
00:00:02,265 --> 00:00:04,805
Everyone on Earth,
holding hands.

3
00:00:05,725 --> 00:00:07,820
Stretch your arms
out wide.

4
00:00:07,875 --> 00:00:10,230
You are about as wide
as you are tall.

5
00:00:10,515 --> 00:00:12,130
Call
it a meter and a half,

6
00:00:12,130 --> 00:00:14,415
for grown-ups
and kids together.

7
00:00:15,320 --> 00:00:17,640
Now add all
8 billion people,

8
00:00:17,640 --> 00:00:20,060
one after another,
hand in hand.

9
00:00:20,225 --> 00:00:22,715
Out past
the horizon it goes,

10
00:00:22,715 --> 00:00:24,190
until the line is about

11
00:00:24,190 --> 00:00:26,775
12 million kilometers
long.

12
00:00:27,325 --> 00:00:29,430
That number is too
big to picture.

13
00:00:29,590 --> 00:00:31,370
So let's wrap
the line around

14
00:00:31,370 --> 00:00:33,915
something we all know:
the Earth.

15
00:00:34,105 --> 00:00:35,895
Pull it tight,
like a thread.

16
00:00:38,120 --> 00:00:42,175
It circles the Earth
about 310 times.

17
00:00:42,475 --> 00:00:44,450
And one lap needs only

18
00:00:44,450 --> 00:00:47,530
about one person in 300
of us.

19
00:00:50,745 --> 00:00:53,730
Make everyone a little
shorter or taller,

20
00:00:53,850 --> 00:00:55,490
and the chain
still wraps

21
00:00:55,490 --> 00:00:57,415
the Earth
hundreds of times.

22
00:00:58,520 --> 00:01:00,070
The same line
would reach

23
00:01:00,070 --> 00:01:01,885
the Moon again
and again.

24
00:01:02,040 --> 00:01:03,310
We are each small,

25
00:01:03,310 --> 00:01:05,475
but together we
are very long.

26
00:01:10,826 --> 00:01:13,978
If your brain's doing the math with me, tap like and follow.
